1. Open the Configuration Tool:
	• Launch SEBConfigTool.exe (located in the Safe Exam Browser installation folder).
	• Open your existing .seb configuration file or start a new configuration.
2. Configure Permitted Processes (Applications):
	• Navigate to the Applications tab in the left-hand navigation pane.
	• Under Permitted Processes, click the + (Add Application) button or Choose Application... to select the executable file (.exe) of the third-party software you want to allow (e.g., Excel, MATLAB, or a specific tool).
	• Enable the option Icon in task bar for that application so students can easily launch or bring its window to the foreground.
	• Ensure Monitor processes while SEB is running is properly configured so that non-permitted applications are blocked or hidden while allowed apps run.
3. Enable the SEB Taskbar:
	• Go to the User Interface tab.
	• Enable the SEB task bar option so that icons for your permitted third-party applications appear cleanly inside the SEB environment.
4. Save and Distribute:
	• Save the configuration file (.seb) and upload or share it with the exam setup or students.